  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following compound will give blood red colour while doing the Lassaigne&#39;s test for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nfOXq",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kjmgK",
      "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math></p>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yZXV4",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kcKvJ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When nitrogen and sulphur both are present in the organic compound, they combine during fusion to form sodium thiocyanate (sulphocyanide).</p><p>Thus, the compounds containing both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> give blood red colour in Lassaigne&#39;s test due to the formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>SCN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> gives blood red colour in Lassaigne&#39;s test of nitrogen.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
